# Differential cases (ADR-0020) of #82: objects with and without a repeated key, iterated, printed and indexed, around
# the distinct-key object (tag 10, ADR-0002 as amended by F-40: more than 8 keys, all tag 5, none repeated); format:
# oracle/src/main/java/io/github/subapavel/jqj/oracle/diff/DiffCase.java. Expected outputs live in distinct.rec, written
# by scripts/oracle-record.sh only. Ids are immutable. Each object runs .[] . .k0 .k8 .zz with -c.

# The 8-key boundary: 8 distinct keys are not proved, 9 are (tag 10).

case distinct/eight-iterate
arg -c
filter .[]
stdin {"k0":0,"k1":1,"k2":2,"k3":3,"k4":4,"k5":5,"k6":6,"k7":7}\n
end

case distinct/eight-dot
arg -c
filter .
stdin {"k0":0,"k1":1,"k2":2,"k3":3,"k4":4,"k5":5,"k6":6,"k7":7}\n
